   "method": "lidar tier error model. Lengths: sigma = sqrt((v*s)^2 + a^2) with a scale term s = 0.003 shared by every measurement (the larger of the tier floor and the geometry's estimate, with the scale spread across video chunks or the scale error of a rejected loop closure) and additive terms a = 0.008 m (walls), 0.006 m (heights), 0.012 m (openings), 0.020 m (damage), inflated for thin evidence on the measurement and on a wall's two end walls (low observed fraction, few face points, fit residuals in quadrature, low light, fewer than 4 photos or views, missing focal length). A wall ending at a wall with no face of its own may run on by 0.15 of the room's extent along it (at most 3 times the wall's length) and is no shorter than the part of its face that was seen. A wall ending at an unobserved wall or a step (shorter than 0.50 m, or shorter than 1.00 m and low) may be a fragment: its upper bound reaches the pieces beyond the step or the room's extent along the wall. Heights add a vertical term of 0.00 (log); an unobserved floor or ceiling widens the upper side by z*0.50 m, an unobserved ceiling up to 4.0 m; a door with no head edge found reaches down to 1.90 m. Areas: sqrt((2*A*s)^2 + (sum of L_i*a_i)^2) plus unobserved wall positions, and upward to the bounding box when a wall may be a fragment. Footprint: scale term fully correlated across rooms plus independent per-room terms; unplaced rooms widen footprint and extents 1.5x. Interval = value - z*q*sigma to value + z*q*sigma_hi with z = 1.645, the one-sided terms widening only their side, lo clipped at 0; q = 1.00, prior value: not calibrated, this tier has fewer than 9 ground-truth rooms. Wall surface areas combine the length, height and opening intervals by interval arithmetic.",
   "q": 1.0,
   "calibration": "prior"
  },
  "definitions": {
   "wall_length": "face to face at 1 m height between the two neighbouring walls, along the room polygon edge",
